I'm going crazy with this. Let me look at the spec again carefully:

```
"execute": {
  ...
  "parameters": {
    "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "properties": {
      "mode": {...},
      "request": {...},
      "target": {...}
    }
  }
}
```

So execute accepts either `request` or `target`. The `request` is the one I want.

Let me think about what's actually happening. Each of my retried calls is being recorded as an "empty" call to the system. Maybe the format issue is genuine — perhaps writing curly braces inside XML tags is being determined as "self-closing" tags, so my content gets consumed.

Wait, look back: I successfully sent an OAuth call. In that call, I see my input had multi-line content. The system showed my parameters as:
`<request>` then `<protocol>rest</protocol>` etc on their own lines, then `</request>`.

So my input must have followed the format of having raw text between tags, and the system showed the parameters as nested children. Was my input as nested children? Or as a single string?

I don't actually know. Let me try with XML-like nested tag approach for the catalog call.
